Z||000000||sjp777||05-25-2001||11:29 PM||||Total confidence, total domination. They could really be the first team to go undefeated in the playoffs.<P>L.A. now has what Chicago had a couple years ago. Common denominator: Phil Jackson. Yeah, I know the arguement, look at the players he's had. But what other coach can get superstar egos like that to play together as a team? All the bickering between Kobe and Shaq, just like Michael and Scotty in years past. What happens when playoff time rolls around? Egos get put aside and the ass kickin begins.<P>Vive Le Roi<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Fformula88||05-25-2001||11:35 PM||||I was skeptical that Jackson's success was all due to Jordan, but now that he has managed to cool the egos of the Lakers enough to play the playoffs, I am beginning to believe in him.  The Lakers have to be the favorites right now.<P>I'd like to see the 76ers go all the way.  I've been a huge Iverson fan since the day he stepped onto the Georgetown campus!  Actually, I am a huge Hoya fan and tend to root for them in the NBA.  I think a lakers 76ers final would be very interesting... the explosiveness of Iverson and Kobe Bryant with Shaq's dominance versus Motumbo's great "D".  Unfortunately for me, Iverson's injuries may end up costing the 76ers the series.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
